index 000000000..5590b1810
--- /dev/null
+++ b/packages/plus/docs/round3-t3-evidence.md
@@ -0,0 +1,143 @@
+# T3 evidence — protected agents are protected at the API boundary
+
+Status: implemented on this branch. The code and test commit is
+`3f8c3890e16e6f77eb0039f8b06305351588347a` (tree
+`7b691db4d711951b561cc9735053be8614bd118d`); the receipts below were captured
+from the assigned checks at that commit. This file lands in the following
+commit, so the branch tip differs from that commit only by this document.
+
+## What changed
+
+- `packages/plus/src/rpc.ts:640` declares the `Plus.AgentProtected` error
+  `{ agent, id?, reason }`, with `id` reserved for a row/input id distinct
+  from the protected agent. `rpc.ts:980` wraps it for the portable client and
+  every guarded method lists it under `errors` (`rpc.ts:1062`-`1305`).
+- `packages/plus/src/rpc.ts` adds an optional `actor` to `CreateAgentInput`,
+  `RenameAgentInput`, `DeleteAgentInput`, `CreateTeamInput`,
+  `TeamAddAgentInput`, `TeamRemoveAgentInput`, `DeleteTeamInput`,
+  `ModelAddInput`, `ModelRemoveInput`, `RuleAddInput`, `RuleRemoveInput`, and
+  `RuleUpdateInput`. `MutateInput.actor` already existed. A missing actor is
+  the TUI; only `{ type: "tool" }` is refused.
+- `packages/plus/src/index.ts:2301` adds one helper,
+  `refuseProtectedForTool(actor, agentId, config)`. It returns the declared
+  error when the actor is a tool and the addressed owner is listed in
+  `protectedAgents`, and `undefined` otherwise. The refusal message is the
+  same text the tool wrappers raise:
+  `agent.protected: row belongs to protected agent "<id>"`.
+- `packages/plus/src/index.ts` replaces the old unconditional
+  `ruleProtectedRefusal` and the unconditional `agent.create` check with the
+  helper.
+
+## Guard map
+
+| write | owner checked | `index.ts` line |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `instructions.mutate` | first changed record's `agent` (team records skipped) | 452 |
+| `agent.create` | requested id | 550 |
+| `agent.rename` | `from` id | 607 |
+| `agent.rename` | `to` id | 609 |
+| `agent.delete` | requested id | 645 |
+| `team.create` with a template | first protected template member | 936 |
+| `team.addAgent` | member id | 1074 |
+| `team.removeAgent` | member id | 1163 |
+| `team.delete` | first protected member of the discovered team | 1245 |
+| `model.add` | `agent` (null = shared row, allowed) | 1371 |
+| `model.remove` | `agent` | 1464 |
+| `rule.add` | requested `agent` | 1530 |
+| `rule.remove` | matched record's owner | 1610 |
+| `rule.update` | matched record's owner, else the requested `agent` (the upsert only adopts the caller's address when nothing matched) | 1656 |
+
+Model activation is a `model` record with `active: true` sent through
+`instructions.mutate`, so the mutate row above covers add/remove/activate.
+`instructions.mutate` compares `deltaRows(loaded.records, proposedRecords)`:
+a full-snapshot mutate that carries a protected agent's records back unchanged
+is a no-op, not a refusal.
+
+## Test receipts
+
+Assigned check `protected`
+(`bun test test/rpc.test.ts test/tools.test.ts test/teams-rpc.test.ts`,
+cwd `packages/plus`) at commit `3f8c3890`, exit code 0 — excerpt of the lines
+that exercise T3, verbatim from the run:
+
+```
+(pass) protected agents refuse tool-actor agent writes at the RPC boundary and allow TUI writes [8.93ms]
+(pass) protected agents refuse tool-actor model add/remove at the RPC boundary and allow TUI writes [4.48ms]
+(pass) protected agents refuse tool-actor rule writes at the RPC boundary and allow TUI writes [3.96ms]
+(pass) instructions.mutate refuses a tool actor changing a protected agent's row and allows unchanged carries and TUI writes [3.17ms]
+(pass) team.addAgent and team.removeAgent refuse a tool actor on a protected member and allow the TUI [4.13ms]
+(pass) team.delete refuses a tool actor when the team contains a protected member and deletes for the TUI [4.88ms]
+(pass) team.create with a template refuses a tool actor cloning a protected member and seeds for the TUI [2.35ms]
+(pass) protectedAgents refusal on a write [9.95ms]
+(pass) protected agent creation refuses before writing a file or log line [1.92ms]
+(pass) deleting a protected agent's custom rule through another agent's row is refused [21.70ms]
+(pass) removeRule refuses a protected owner's rule for a tool actor and lets the TUI remove it [7.30ms]
+(pass) rule.remove RPC from another agent's row refuses a tool actor and lets the TUI remove it [6.18ms]
+(pass) updating a protected agent's custom rule through another agent's row is refused (tools API) [21.17ms]
+(pass) rule.update RPC from another agent's row refuses a tool actor and lets the TUI write [12.05ms]
+```
+
+Run tail, verbatim:
+
+```
+ 140 pass
+ 4 skip
+ 0 fail
+ 1120 expect() calls
+Ran 144 tests across 3 files. [1.65s]
+```
+
+Assigned check `typecheck` (`bun run typecheck`, cwd `packages/plus`) at the
+same commit, exit code 0:
+
+```
+$ tsgo --noEmit -p tsconfig.test.json
+```
+
+## What the tests prove
+
+- `test/rpc.test.ts` "protected agents refuse tool-actor agent writes…":
+  `agent.create` with a tool actor fails `agent.protected` with the exact
+  message and leaves `<project>/.opencode/agent/alpha.md` absent; the same
+  call without an actor writes it. `agent.delete` and both `agent.rename`
+  directions are refused for a tool actor with the source file and the target
+  path unchanged, while the TUI rename and delete succeed.
+- `test/rpc.test.ts` "protected agents refuse tool-actor model add/remove…":
+  the refused `model.add` leaves `records` empty; the TUI add persists; the
+  refused `model.remove` leaves the model record present; the TUI remove
+  deletes it.
+- `test/rpc.test.ts` "protected agents refuse tool-actor rule writes…":
+  refused `rule.add`/`rule.update`/`rule.remove` leave the stored label
+  unchanged and the record present; the TUI add/edit/remove through another
+  agent's row succeed with the owner staying `alpha`.
+- `test/rpc.test.ts` "instructions.mutate refuses a tool actor…": a tool
+  mutate carrying the protected row unchanged succeeds as a no-op; the same
+  tool mutate with `text: "second"` fails `agent.protected` and the stored
+  text stays `"first"`; the TUI mutate writes `"second"`.
+- `test/teams-rpc.test.ts` covers `team.addAgent`, `team.removeAgent`,
+  `team.delete`, and `team.create` with a template: each tool-actor call is
+  refused with `agent.protected` and writes no member file, and the same call
+  without an actor succeeds.
+- `test/tools.test.ts` "removeRule refuses a protected owner's rule for a tool
+  actor and lets the TUI remove it" and the `rule.remove`/`rule.update` RPC
+  tests assert the refusal type `agent.protected` in the throwing context
+  double, the exact log-file prefix unchanged across the refusal
+  (`logLines(project)` equality), and the TUI call then writing the row and
+  appending a log line. The pre-existing tool-wrapper tests
+  (`protectedAgents refusal on a write`, `protected agent creation refuses
+  before writing a file or log line`, `deleting a protected agent's custom
+  rule…`, `updating a protected agent's custom rule…`) are unchanged and
+  still pass, so the early tool refusal and its error text are preserved.
+
+No capture above is a mock: every case drives the real handlers
+(`createHandlers`/`createPlusApi`) against a temporary project directory and
+asserts stored files, snapshot records, and the append-only log.
+
+## Boundaries respected
+
+- T2's `message` field semantics are untouched: the `message` key on
+  `RuleAddInput`/`RuleUpdateInput` and `RuleRecord` is unchanged; the T2
+  message tests (`rule.add and rule.update accept an optional refusal
+  message…`, `updateRule … message`) still pass.
+- T6 search keys and the `server:search` query filter are untouched.
+- No file outside `packages/plus` was modified for this task.
\ No newline at end of file
